# The analysis frame's own version, and the only place it is written.
#
# YYYYMMDD.NNN - the day it changed, then a counter from 001 for that day. Commit the bump with
# the change it describes: every intermediate's provenance record carries this, and it is what
# tells a later run that an intermediate was derived by code that no longer computes the same
# thing.
#
# dev/scripts/check-analysis-versions.sh compares the DAY, so one bump covers a day's changes.
#
# BUMP IT FOR: analysis/frame.config, and anything under analysis/lib/. Those are what a module
# imports and what it runs under, so a change to either can change what a derivation produces.
#
# DO NOT BUMP FOR: analysis/modules-index.tsv, which is the catalogue of downloadable modules -
# it does not ship, no derivation reads it, and it changes whenever anyone publishes a module.
# Nor for a module under analysis/modules/, which carries its own version in its manifest.json.
# Nor for analysis.nf, 0_verify_analysis.nf, modules.nf or complete.nf: they verify, report and
# move files, and a module imports none of them.
#
# A change in scripts/ CAN reach a derivation, because analysis/lib/nf/plan.nf imports
# resolve_parameters.nf and variants.nf. That one is caught elsewhere: the pipeline release
# moves with it, and the identity check refuses results produced by a different release.
#
# It is NOT the pipeline release and does not move with it, so dev/scripts/bump-version.sh does
# not touch this file. Each module carries its own version in the same form, in its manifest.json.
#
# Blank lines and lines starting with # are ignored; the first line left is the version.
20260902.001
